/S /H1
/T (Types of Streaking Methods Several streaking techniques are employed in microbiology laboratories depending on the type of sample and purpose of culture. a\) Zig-Zag Streaking Method In this method, the inoculum is streaked in a continuous zig-zag pattern across the agar surface. It is mainly used for urine samples and situations where quantitative or semi-quantitative growth assessment is required. Advantages: Simple and quick method Useful for observing overall bacterial growth Limitations: Less effective in obtaining well-isolated colonies)
/E (Types of Streaking Methods Several streaking techniques are employed in microbiology laboratories depending on the type of sample and purpose of culture. a\) Zig-Zag Streaking Method In this method, the inoculum is streaked in a continuous zig-zag pattern across the agar surface. It is mainly used for urine samples and situations where quantitative or semi-quantitative growth assessment is required. Advantages: Simple and quick method Useful for observing overall bacterial growth Limitations: Less effective in obtaining well-isolated colonies)
